<body>

<!-- HEADER -->
<header class="report-header">
  <div class="container">
    <h1>BIEK Computer Science 12th Class &mdash; Past Paper Trend Analysis</h1>
    <div class="subtitle">11 Years of Examination Patterns (2015&ndash;2025) &middot; HSC Part-2 Paper-II</div>
    <div class="meta">Board of Intermediate Education Karachi &bull; Community-Compiled Question Bank &bull; 327 Questions Analyzed</div>
  </div>
</header>

<div class="container">

<!-- ===== SECTION 1: OVERVIEW ===== -->
<section id="overview">
  <h2>1. Dataset &amp; Examination Overview</h2>

  <div class="kpi-row">
    <div class="kpi-card">
      <div class="kpi-value">327</div>
      <div class="kpi-label">Total Questions</div>
    </div>
    <div class="kpi-card alt">
      <div class="kpi-value">10</div>
      <div class="kpi-label">Years with Data (2015&ndash;2025)</div>
    </div>
    <div class="kpi-card warn">
      <div class="kpi-value">2020</div>
      <div class="kpi-label">Year Missing from Dataset</div>
    </div>
    <div class="kpi-card">
      <div class="kpi-value">3</div>
      <div class="kpi-label">Question Types</div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="card">
    <p>This analysis covers <strong>327 examination questions</strong> from the BIEK Computer Science Paper-II (HSC Part-2 / Intermediate Second Year) spanning <strong>10 examination years</strong> between 2015 and 2025. The dataset was sourced from a community-compiled question bank based on official BIEK past papers.</p>
    <p style="margin-top:10px;">The year <strong>2020 is absent</strong> from the dataset, likely due to examination disruptions during the COVID-19 pandemic. All findings and trend lines explicitly skip 2020; no interpolation or imputation has been applied.</p>

    <h3>Overall Question Type Distribution</h3>
    <table>
      <thead><tr><th>Question Type</th><th>Count</th><th>Share of Total</th><th>Per-Year Average</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td><span class="tag mcq">MCQs</span></td><td>150</td><td>45.9%</td><td>15.0</td></tr>
        <tr><td><span class="tag short">Short</span></td><td>147</td><td>44.9%</td><td>14.7</td></tr>
        <tr><td><span class="tag long">Long</span></td><td>30</td><td>9.2%</td><td>3.0</td></tr>
        <tr style="font-weight:700"><td>Total</td><td>327</td><td>100.0%</td><td>32.7</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <p class="footnote">MCQs are Multiple Choice Questions (typically 4 options). Short Questions require brief explanations or definitions. Long Questions are essay-type with multiple sub-parts.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ===== SECTION 2: YEARLY DISTRIBUTION ===== -->
<section id="yearly-distribution">
  <h2>2. Year-by-Year Question Volume Analysis</h2>

  <div class="card">
    <h3>Questions per Year</h3>
    <table>
      <thead><tr><th>Year</th><th>MCQs</th><th>Short</th><th>Long</th><th>Total</th><th>YoY Change</th><th>YoY %</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>2015</td><td>15</td><td>9</td><td>3</td><td>27</td><td>&mdash;</td><td>&mdash;</td></tr>
        <tr><td>2016</td><td>15</td><td>9</td><td>3</td><td>27</td><td>0</td><td>0.0%</td></tr>
        <tr><td>2017</td><td>15</td><td>18</td><td>3</td><td>36</td><td>+9</td><td>+33.3%</td></tr>
        <tr><td>2018</td><td>15</td><td>18</td><td>3</td><td>36</td><td>0</td><td>0.0%</td></tr>
        <tr><td>2019</td><td>15</td><td>18</td><td>3</td><td>36</td><td>0</td><td>0.0%</td></tr>
        <tr><td>2020</td><td colspan="4" style="text-align:center;font-style:italic;color:#95a5a6">No data (COVID-19 disruption)</td><td>&mdash;</td><td>&mdash;</td></tr>
        <tr><td>2021</td><td>15</td><td>15</td><td>3</td><td>33</td><td>&mdash;</td><td>&mdash;</td></tr>
        <tr><td>2022</td><td>15</td><td>15</td><td>3</td><td>33</td><td>0</td><td>0.0%</td></tr>
        <tr><td>2023</td><td>15</td><td>15</td><td>3</td><td>33</td><td>0</td><td>0.0%</td></tr>
        <tr><td>2024</td><td>15</td><td>15</td><td>3</td><td>33</td><td>0</td><td>0.0%</td></tr>
        <tr><td>2025</td><td>15</td><td>15</td><td>3</td><td>33</td><td>0</td><td>0.0%</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <p class="footnote">YoY change is computed only between consecutive years with data. The 2019&rarr;2021 gap is not compared due to the missing 2020.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="card">
    <h3>Total Questions per Year</h3>
    <div class="chart-wrap" style="height:360px">
      <canvas id="chartYearlyTotal"></canvas>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="insight warn">
    <strong>Key Finding:</strong> The most significant structural shift occurred in <strong>2017</strong>, when Short Questions doubled from 9 to 18, increasing total questions by 33.3%. From 2021 onward, the exam has stabilized at 33 questions (15 MCQs + 15 Short + 3 Long), a structure distinct from the earlier 2015&ndash;2016 format.
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ===== SECTION 3: QUESTION TYPE COMPOSITION ===== -->
<section id="question-type-analysis">
  <h2>3. Question Type Composition &amp; Trends</h2>

  <div class="card">
    <h3>Stacked Question Volume by Year</h3>
    <div class="chart-wrap" style="height:420px">
      <canvas id="chartStackedBar"></canvas>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="card">
    <h3>Question Type Share Over Time</h3>
    <div class="chart-wrap" style="height:400px">
      <canvas id="chartTypePercent"></canvas>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="card">
    <h3>Stability Assessment</h3>
    <table>
      <thead><tr><th>Metric</th><th>MCQs</th><th>Short</th><th>Long</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>Count range across years</td><td>15 &ndash; 15</td><td>9 &ndash; 18</td><td>3 &ndash; 3</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Standard deviation</td><td>0.0</td><td>3.5</td><td>0.0</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Most common count</td><td>15 (all years)</td><td>15 (5 years)</td><td>3 (all years)</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Stability verdict</td><td>Fully stable</td><td>Shifted in 2017, re-stabilized 2021</td><td>Fully stable</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <div class="insight info">
    <strong>Structural Shift Pattern:</strong> Three distinct eras emerge: <strong>Era 1 (2015&ndash;2016)</strong> with 27 questions (15+9+3); <strong>Era 2 (2017&ndash;2019)</strong> with 36 questions (15+18+3), where Short Questions doubled; and <strong>Era 3 (2021&ndash;2025)</strong> settling at 33 questions (15+15+3), a middle ground. MCQs and Long Questions have remained completely unchanged throughout.
  </div>

  <div class="card">
    <h3>Question Type Ratio by Year</h3>
    <table>
      <thead><tr><th>Year</th><th>MCQs %</th><th>Short %</th><th>Long %</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>2015</td><td>55.6%</td><td>33.3%</td><td>11.1%</td></tr>
        <tr><td>2016</td><td>55.6%</td><td>33.3%</td><td>11.1%</td></tr>
        <tr><td>2017</td><td>41.7%</td><td>50.0%</td><td>8.3%</td></tr>
        <tr><td>2018</td><td>41.7%</td><td>50.0%</td><td>8.3%</td></tr>
        <tr><td>2019</td><td>41.7%</td><td>50.0%</td><td>8.3%</td></tr>
        <tr><td>2021</td><td>45.5%</td><td>45.5%</td><td>9.1%</td></tr>
        <tr><td>2022</td><td>45.5%</td><td>45.5%</td><td>9.1%</td></tr>
        <tr><td>2023</td><td>45.5%</td><td>45.5%</td><td>9.1%</td></tr>
        <tr><td>2024</td><td>45.5%</td><td>45.5%</td><td>9.1%</td></tr>
        <tr><td>2025</td><td>45.5%</td><td>45.5%</td><td>9.1%</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ===== SECTION 4: TOPIC PATTERNS ===== -->
<section id="topic-patterns">
  <h2>4. Recurring Topics &amp; Question Content Patterns</h2>

  <div class="card">
    <p>A keyword and content analysis was performed on all 327 question texts. Each question was classified into one or more topic categories based on its substantive content. The <code>$</code> delimiter in MCQ options and Long Question sub-parts was accounted for during text preprocessing. Below are the identified topic clusters ranked by frequency.</p>

    <h3>Topic Frequency Across All Years</h3>
    <div id="topicBars"></div>
  </div>

  <div class="card">
    <h3>Topic Frequency by Year (Heatmap Data)</h3>
    <div class="chart-wrap" style="height:520px">
      <canvas id="chartTopicHeatmap"></canvas>
    </div>
    <p class="footnote">Counts reflect the number of questions tagged with each topic category per year. A single question may cover multiple topics, so column totals may exceed the actual question count.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="card">
    <h3>Most Recurring Specific Questions &amp; Themes</h3>
    <p>Certain question themes appear with remarkable consistency across nearly every examination year. These represent the highest-yield areas for exam preparation:</p>
    <table>
      <thead><tr><th>Recurring Theme</th><th>Years Appeared</th><th>Frequency</th><th>Types</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>While vs. do-while loop differences</td><td>2015, 2017, 2019</td><td>3</td><td><span class="tag short">Short</span></td></tr>
        <tr><td>Full forms of DML, DDL, SQL, RDBMS, DBA</td><td>2015, 2017, 2018, 2019</td><td>4</td><td><span class="tag short">Short</span></td></tr>
        <tr><td>DBMS advantages</td><td>2015, 2019, 2021</td><td>3</td><td><span class="tag short">Short</span><span class="tag long">Long</span></td></tr>
        <tr><td>Primary key vs. Foreign key distinction</td><td>2017, 2019, 2021</td><td>3</td><td><span class="tag short">Short</span><span class="tag mcq">MCQ</span></td></tr>
        <tr><td>Program output prediction (tracing)</td><td>2017, 2018, 2019, 2021, 2022, 2023, 2024, 2025</td><td>8</td><td><span class="tag short">Short</span></td></tr>
        <tr><td>Writing C programs (area, tables, sums)</td><td>2015, 2016, 2017, 2019, 2021, 2023, 2024, 2025</td><td>8</td><td><span class="tag short">Short</span></td></tr>
        <tr><td>Mathematical expression conversion to C</td><td>2015, 2016, 2018, 2019</td><td>4</td><td><span class="tag short">Short</span></td></tr>
        <tr><td>Valid/invalid identifier identification</td><td>2016, 2018, 2019</td><td>3</td><td><span class="tag short">Short</span></td></tr>
        <tr><td>Database models (explanation)</td><td>2015, 2017, 2019, 2022, 2023, 2025</td><td>6</td><td><span class="tag long">Long</span></td></tr>
        <tr><td>Functions &amp; recursion (explanation)</td><td>2015, 2017, 2019, 2022, 2023, 2024, 2025</td><td>7</td><td><span class="tag long">Long</span><span class="tag short">Short</span></td></tr>
