  <div class="card">
    <h3>Format-Specific Strategies</h3>

    <h3>MCQs (15 questions every year &mdash; 100% predictable count)</h3>
    <p>MCQs test factual recall and concept identification. The most tested MCQ categories are:</p>
    <ul style="margin-left:24px;margin-bottom:14px;">
      <li><strong>Operator identification</strong> (logical AND &amp;&amp;, OR ||, NOT !, modulus %, increment ++, etc.) &mdash; appears virtually every year</li>
      <li><strong>Format specifier matching</strong> (%d, %f, %c, %s, %lf, %ld) &mdash; appears every year</li>
      <li><strong>Database terminology</strong> (tuple, attribute, primary key, foreign key, DBMS) &mdash; appears every year</li>
      <li><strong>Data type sizes</strong> (int 2 bytes, float 4 bytes, char 1 byte, double 8 bytes) &mdash; appears most years</li>
      <li><strong>MS Access object identification</strong> (Table, Query, Form, Report) &mdash; appears most years</li>
    </ul>

    <h3>Short Questions (15 questions since 2021 &mdash; most variable section)</h3>
    <p>Short Questions test both recall and application. Expect:</p>
    <ul style="margin-left:24px;margin-bottom:14px;">
      <li><strong>1&ndash;2 program-writing tasks</strong> (area calculations, number series, loops)</li>
      <li><strong>1 output prediction question</strong> (trace a loop or conditional)</li>
      <li><strong>1&ndash;2 definition/comparison questions</strong> (while vs. do-while, primary vs. foreign key)</li>
      <li><strong>1 database concept</strong> (keys, relationships, DBA role)</li>
    </ul>

    <h3>Long Questions (3 questions every year &mdash; 100% predictable count)</h3>
    <p>Each Long Question contains 2&ndash;3 sub-parts spanning C programming and database topics. The pattern is remarkably consistent:</p>
    <ul style="margin-left:24px;">
      <li><strong>Question 3:</strong> Typically covers control structures/loops + a C concept + a database concept</li>
      <li><strong>Question 4:</strong> Typically covers a C program + operators/I/O/functions + a DBMS/RDBMS concept</li>
      <li><strong>Question 5:</strong> Typically covers functions/recursion + control structures + MS Access/normalization</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

